  message: "FIXED ON A LOCAL BRANCH, NOT INTEGRATED (2026-10-04). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/lopus (worktree ~/hg_wt/lopus), based on stage-8 2a98abb55d. Commit 57d10d835f. Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/lopus.md.\n\nPREMISE RE-VERIFIED, AND THE MECHANISM IS NARROWER THAN FILED: each gatling site is a subclass (FirstPassParser / SecondPassParser) calling LogFileParser's own protected readInt / readLong / readBoolean / readByte as a bare name. The scala analyzer emits an `external` stub AND the inherited-calls linker emits the resolved edge to LogFileParser.readInt for the same call; finalize stamps meta.superseded_by on the stub (ADR-0057 §14). The row choice never read the stamp.\n\nFIX, AT THE ROW-CHOICE LAYER FOR BOTH CONSUMERS (INV-foda): io_boundary.short_name_fallback_withheld(dst, meta) -- a first-party callable dst, or a superseded stub -- withholds the gate arm of named_lookup_arm. classify_call_in_catalog passes it as allow_short_name_fallback; taint's _match_propagation_entry hands it to _lookup_named_entry. Qualified and module arms untouched. ambiguous_names was NOT used: it cannot tell these stubs from a genuine `import scala.io.StdIn._; readInt()`, which carries no superseder and still classifies (pinned).\n\nEVIDENCE: io-boundaries A/B by chain (arm A exported 2a98abb55d, arm B branch): gatling 3712 -> 3697, the 15 removed are every scala.io.StdIn chain in the repo, all in LogFileReader.scala subclass methods (read each: readInt x9, readBoolean x4, readLong x1, readByte x1); 0 added. sbt 3984 -> 3984, http4s 1625 -> 1625, pekko 20255 -> 20255; pekko's two genuine StdIn.readLine reads (EchoServer.scala, TwitterStreamQuickstartDocSpec.scala via import scala.io.StdIn.readLine) remain. hypergumbo self-claims: 18/18 confirmed_with_caveats in both arms, caveat kinds identical.\n\nRESIDUAL, FILED: pekko GzipDecompressor.scala:47 `import reader._; readByte()` (reader: ByteStringParser.ByteReader, pekko's own class) still reads as StdIn.readByte, because nothing in the graph binds it in-repo -- WI-nusol-rohih-zurus-votul-korus-zupoj-zutav-vunor. So the title's general condition is NOT asserted closed; the filed gatling instance is."  # b748
